# Reject grammar-invalid draft tokens in the V2 (worker/gpu) runner. The
# scheduler marks grammar-rejected drafts with -1 sentinels
# (scheduler_output.num_invalid_spec_tokens), but the V2 runner takes drafts
# from req_states.draft_tokens on the GPU and never sees the sentinels, so
# the rejection sampler can accept grammar-illegal drafts and the structured
# output manager AssertionErrors the engine (vllm#46118, vllm#49694). Mirror
# the V1 runner: scatter the sentinels into the batch, keep a pre-clamp
# gather for the rejection sampler, downgrade the assert to a warning.
#
# Carried from confidential-glm5-2-b200 (vLLM v0.27.0); rebased onto
# ZJY0516/vllm@933876c (glm-release, vllm#53906; image
# vllm/vllm-openai:glm53-flash): line offsets regenerated, and InputBatch
# gained a max_query_len kwarg/field — our draft_sampled_raw kwarg/field now
# sits after it. Retire when fixed upstream.
